# VR debug logging

All VR diagnostic / debug output must go through `VrDiagLog` so it appears in **both** the Godot console and the session log files.

## Do

```csharp
VrDiagLog.Print("[VR] …");
VrDiagLog.Warn("[VR] …");
VrDiagLog.Debug("[TMAP] …"); // alias of Print
```

## Do not

```csharp
GD.Print("[VR] …");           // console only — forbidden for VR diagnostics
Debug.Print("[VR] …");        // debugger only — forbidden for VR diagnostics
```

## Log locations

| Path | When |
|------|------|
| `logs/vr_diag.log` | Workspace (agent-readable) |
| `%APPDATA%/Godot/app_userdata/Underworld/vr_diag.log` | Godot `user://` |

Native VR (`vr: true`, not `vr_mirror`) always mirrors `VrDiagLog` to these files. Prefer prefixes like `[VR]`, `[TMAP]`, `[VR combat]`, `[MISSILE-DIAG]` for grepping.

